To give full read, write, and execute permissions to all users for a folder in Ubuntu, you use the chmod command with the 777 or a+rwx permission setting. [1, 2] 
Open your terminal (Ctrl + Alt + T) and run one of the options below:
## Option 1: Apply to the folder only
If you want to grant access only to the specific folder (leaving existing files inside unchanged), run: [1, 3] 

sudo chmod 777 /path/to/your/folder

## Option 2: Apply to the folder and everything inside (Recommended)
If you want to grant full permissions to the folder, all of its subfolders, and all files currently inside it, add the -R (recursive) flag: [1, 4] 

sudo chmod -R 777 /path/to/your/folder

