## What do these components mean?

* 
* sudo: Runs the command with root administrator privileges (required if you don't own the folder). [2] 
* -R: Short for recursive. It forces the changes down into every sub-folder and file. [1, 4] 
* 777: The numeric notation for full access.
* The first 7 gives full rights (Read + Write + Execute) to the Owner.
   * The second 7 gives full rights to the Group.
   * The third 7 gives full rights to Everyone else (all other users). [2, 5] 
* 

⚠️ Security Note: Granting 777 permissions means any user or program on the system can modify, delete, or run files in that directory. Avoid using this on system folders or critical environment paths. [3, 5] 
